  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nA mid level ridge centered over the southeast U.S. extending north\ninto the Ohio Valley will offer dry and very warm conditions today. \n\nWell above normal temperatures are expected for today with highs\nfrom the mid 80s north to the upper 80s south. Can not rule out the\npotential for a 90 degree high at a valley location near and south of\nthe Ohio River. \n\nTemperatures will fall on Friday as a cold front accompanied by rain\nmoves south through the Ohio Valley. This will usher in below normal\ntemperatures for the remainder of the week. There will be the \npotential for some patchy frost Monday night into Tuesday morning.\n\n\nKey Message 2)\n\nA slow moving front will move into the area tonight. Showers which \ndevelop into west central Ohio this evening will overspread the\nentire area overnight as the front slips south. Showers will persist\non Friday as a weak wave of low pressure ripples along the front. \nForecast soundings show very marginal instability - so can not rule\nout embedded thunder. Also, brief periods of heavy rain will be \npossible with moisture returning and PWATs approaching 2 inches. \nExpect a widespread rainfall of 0.5 to 1 inch with some locally\nhigher amounts before ending by Friday evening.",
